      "description": "A line of light along the spine, brightest at its core and dissipating into a soft bloom either side. It breaks in places - a lantern horse rarely carries an unbroken line - and the same colour shows faintly through the mane where the line passes under it. One copy is as lit as two: the horse cannot turn it off, and in the dark it is the only part of it you see.",
